// @run
// @log -1
// @log 1
// @log 42
// A FAILED GROWTH RETURNS -1 AND CHANGES NOTHING. wasm32 caps linear memory at
// 65536 pages (4 GiB), so a request for 70000 more cannot be satisfied. The spec
// says the instruction then evaluates to -1 rather than trapping, and VL passes
// that through unchanged — it does not translate the sentinel, so a program
// checks it exactly as the spec describes.
//
// The two lines after it are the ones that matter: the memory is still one page,
// and the bytes already in it are untouched. A failed grow is not a partial one.
print(__memory_grow__(70000))
print(__memory_size__())
__store_i32__(0, 42)
print(__load_i32__(0))
